# The functions outside we_lineend.c that turn rows into bytes with a line
# break of their own.  Checked by tests/check-line-ends.sh.
#
#   file|function|count|pass|reason
#
# "count" is how many line-break puts or stores the function has; it may
# only fall.  "pass" is the pass that moves the function onto the owner's
# e_eol_text, or:
#   protocol   not the file: a wire format that keys its positions on rows
#              (the language server's document), and stays
#   keep       not a serialiser: it names rows and a '\n' for another reason
#
# L-a1 moved the file writer and the file reader into the owner, L-a2 the
# assistant's four.  The rest of the nine row serialisers of HEAD are here
# until their pass.

we_ai_ws.c|ws_window_text|1|L-b|the model's workspace copy of a window
we_block.c|e_block_to_text|1|L-b|the OS clipboard's copy of a block
we_buffer.c|e_buffer_to_text|1|L-b|the clipboard export and the model's copy
we_lsp.c|e_lsp_join_lines|1|protocol|one server line per buffer row, the server's positions are keyed on rows, soft rows included
we_prog.c|e_p_cmp_mess|1|keep|builds a pattern to match compiler messages, not a file
